{"id":"mahabharata-11-008","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":8,"title":"अष्टमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 8 · Vyasa consoles Dhritarashtra","summary":{"en":"Hearing Vidura, Dhritarashtra falls senseless, and Vyasa comes and tells him that all this was fated and that he himself had foreseen it. Vyasa tells him of the dharma of grief and counsels him to rule with the Pandavas.","kn":"ವಿದುರನ ಮಾತು ಕೇಳಿ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಮೂರ್ಛೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಬಂದು ಇದೆಲ್ಲ ವಿಧಿ, ತಾನೇ ಇದನ್ನು ಮುಂದೆ ಕಂಡಿದ್ದೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಶೋಕದ ಧರ್ಮವನ್ನು ಹೇಳಿ ಪಾಂಡವರೊಡನೆ ಆಳಲು ಸಲಹೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"विदुर की बात सुनकर धृतराष्ट्र मूर्छित हो जाते हैं, और व्यास आकर कहते हैं कि यह सब नियति थी और उन्होंने इसे पहले ही देख लिया था। वे शोक का धर्म बताते हैं और पाण्डवों के साथ राज करने की सलाह देते हैं।","te":"విదురుని మాటలు విని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు మూర్ఛపోతాడు; వ్యాసుడు వచ్చి ఇదంతా విధి అని, తానే దీన్ని ముందుగా చూశానని చెబుతాడు. శోక ధర్మాన్ని చెప్పి పాండవులతో కలిసి పాలించమని సలహా ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"விதுரரின் சொற்களைக் கேட்டு த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் மயங்க, வியாசர் வந்து இதெல்லாம் விதி, தாமே இதை முன்கண்டதாகக் கூறுகிறார். துயரின் தர்மத்தைச் சொல்லிப் பாண்டவருடன் ஆளும்படி அறிவுரைக்கிறார்.","ml":"വിദുരരുടെ വാക്കുകൾ കേട്ട് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ബോധരഹിതനാകുന്നു; വ്യാസൻ വന്ന് ഇതെല്ലാം വിധിച്ചതാണെന്നും താൻ അത് മുൻകൂട്ടി കണ്ടിരുന്നുവെന്നും പറയുന്നു. ദുഃഖത്തിന്റെ ധർമ്മത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുന്ന അദ്ദേഹം, പാണ്ഡവരോടൊപ്പം രാജ്യം ഭരിക്കാൻ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.8; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"जलप्रदानिकपर्व","titleEn":"Jalapradanika Parva (The water offerings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विदुरस्य तु तद्वाक्यं निशम्य कुरुसत्तमः ।\nपुत्रशोकाभिसंतप्तः पपात भुवि मूर्छितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Vidura's words, the best of the Kurus, burning with grief for his sons, fell fainting to the ground."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं तथा पतितं भूमौ निःसंज्ञं प्रेक्ष्य बान्धवाः ।\nकृष्णद्वैपायनश्चैव क्षत्ता च विदुरस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him lying there senseless, his kinsmen, Krishna Dvaipayana, the counselor Vidura,"}},{"n":3,"text":"संजयः सुहृदश्चान्ये द्वाःस्था ये चास्य संमताः ।\nजलेन सुखशीतेन तालवृन्तैश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, other friends, and the trusted gatekeepers sprinkled him with pleasantly cool water and fanned him with palm-leaf fans, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":4,"text":"पस्पृशुश्च करैर्गात्रं वीजमानाश्च यत्नतः ।\nअन्वासन्सुचिरं कालं धृतराष्ट्रं तथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They touched his body with their hands and fanned him diligently, and they sat with Dhritarashtra a long time as he lay in that state."}},{"n":5,"text":"अथ दीर्घस्य कालस्य लब्धसंज्ञो महीपतिः ।\nविललाप चिरं कालं पुत्राधिभिरभिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long while the king regained consciousness and lamented for a long time, flooded with anxiety for his sons."}},{"n":6,"text":"धिगस्तु खलु मानुष्यं मानुष्ये च परिग्रहम् ।\nयतोमूलानि दुःखानि संभवन्ति मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on human life, and shame on human possessions, from which sorrows arise again and again."}},{"n":7,"text":"पुत्रनाशेऽर्थनाशे च ज्ञातिसंबन्धिनामपि ।\nप्राप्यते सुमहद्दुःखं विषाग्निप्रतिमं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, in the loss of sons, of wealth, and of relatives and in-laws, one suffers a very great pain like poison and fire."}},{"n":8,"text":"येन दह्यन्ति गात्राणि येन प्रज्ञा विनश्यति ।\nयेनाभिभूतः पुरुषो मरणं बहु मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It burns the body, it destroys the mind, and overcome by it a man thinks well of death."}},{"n":9,"text":"तदिदं व्यसनं प्राप्तं मया भाग्यविपर्ययात् ।\nतच्चैवाहं करिष्यामि अद्यैव द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This calamity has come upon me through a reversal of fortune, best of brahmins, and I will do that very thing, die, today itself."}},{"n":10,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा तु महात्मानं पितरं ब्रह्मवित्तमम् ।\nधृतराष्ट्रोऽभवन्मूढः शोकं च परमं गतः ।\nअभूच्च तूष्णीं राजासौ ध्यायमानो महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to his father, the great-souled best of Brahman-knowers, Dhritarashtra fell into bewilderment and utmost grief, and the king fell silent, brooding."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा कृष्णद्वैपायनः प्रभुः ।\nपुत्रशोकाभिसंतप्तं पुत्रं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, the lord Krishna Dvaipayana spoke to his son, who was burning with grief for his sons."}},{"n":12,"text":"धृतराष्ट्र महाबाहो यत्त्वां वक्ष्यामि तच्छृणु ।\nश्रुतवानसि मेधावी धर्मार्थकुशलस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra, mighty-armed, hear what I will tell you. You are learned and intelligent, and skilled in dharma and in worldly aims."}},{"n":13,"text":"न तेऽस्त्यविदितं किंचिद्वेदितव्यं परंतप ।\nअनित्यतां हि मर्त्यानां विजानासि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is nothing you do not know, nothing left to be learned, tormentor of foes. You surely understand the impermanence of mortals."}},{"n":14,"text":"अध्रुवे जीवलोके च स्थाने वाशाश्वते सति ।\nजीविते मरणान्ते च कस्माच्छोचसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this uncertain world of the living, where nothing stays and all ends in death, why do you grieve, descendant of Bharata?"}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रत्यक्षं तव राजेन्द्र वैरस्यास्य समुद्भवः ।\nपुत्रं ते कारणं कृत्वा कालयोगेन कारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You saw with your own eyes, great king, how this enmity arose; it was brought about through the course of Time, with your son as the cause."}},{"n":16,"text":"अवश्यं भवितव्ये च कुरूणां वैशसे नृप ।\nकस्माच्छोचसि ताञ्शूरान्गतान्परमिकां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since the destruction of the Kurus was bound to be, king, why do you grieve for those heroes who have gone to the highest goal?"}},{"n":17,"text":"जानता च महाबाहो विदुरेण महात्मना ।\nयतितं सर्वयत्नेन शमं प्रति जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great-souled Vidura, who knew this, strove with every effort for peace, lord of men."}},{"n":18,"text":"न च दैवकृतो मार्गः शक्यो भूतेन केनचित् ।\nघटतापि चिरं कालं नियन्तुमिति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But no one, however long he strives, can hold back the course ordained by fate. That is my view."}},{"n":19,"text":"देवतानां हि यत्कार्यं मया प्रत्यक्षतः श्रुतम् ।\nतत्तेऽहं संप्रवक्ष्यामि कथं स्थैर्यं भवेत्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you what I myself heard directly about the work of the gods, so that you may be steady."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुराहं त्वरितो यातः सभामैन्द्रीं जितक्लमः ।\nअपश्यं तत्र च तदा समवेतान्दिवौकसः ।\nनारदप्रमुखांश्चापि सर्वान्देवऋषींस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once I went in haste to the court of Indra, my weariness conquered, and there I saw the gods assembled, and all the divine sages led by Narada."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत्र चापि मया दृष्टा पृथिवी पृथिवीपते ।\nकार्यार्थमुपसंप्राप्ता देवतानां समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too, king, I saw the Earth, come before the gods on some business."}},{"n":22,"text":"उपगम्य तदा धात्री देवानाह समागतान् ।\nयत्कार्यं मम युष्माभिर्ब्रह्मणः सदने तदा ।\nप्रतिज्ञातं महाभागास्तच्छीघ्रं संविधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Approaching, the Earth, the supporter, said to the gathered gods: \"The task you promised me in Brahma's hall, great ones, let it be accomplished quickly.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्यास्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा विष्णुर्लोकनमस्कृतः ।\nउवाच प्रहसन्वाक्यं पृथिवीं देवसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing her words, Vishnu, to whom the worlds bow, laughed and said to the Earth in the divine assembly:"}},{"n":24,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्राणां यस्तु ज्येष्ठः शतस्य वै ।\nदुर्योधन इति ख्यातः स ते कार्यं करिष्यति ।\nतं च प्राप्य महीपालं कृतकृत्या भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The eldest of Dhritarashtra's hundred sons, famed as Duryodhana, will do your task. When you have obtained that king, your purpose will be done."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्यार्थे पृथिवीपालाः कुरुक्षेत्रे समागताः ।\nअन्योन्यं घातयिष्यन्ति दृढैः शस्त्रैः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For his sake the earth's kings will gather at Kurukshetra and strike one another down with strong weapons."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततस्ते भविता देवि भारस्य युधि नाशनम् ।\nगच्छ शीघ्रं स्वकं स्थानं लोकान्धारय शोभने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, goddess, your burden will be removed in battle. Go quickly to your own place, fair one, and sustain the worlds.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"स एष ते सुतो राजँल्लोकसंहारकारणात् ।\nकलेरंशः समुत्पन्नो गान्धार्या जठरे नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, that son of yours, born in Gandhari's womb, is a portion of Kali, born to bring about the destruction of the worlds."}},{"n":28,"text":"अमर्षी चपलश्चापि क्रोधनो दुष्प्रसाधनः ।\nदैवयोगात्समुत्पन्ना भ्रातरश्चास्य तादृशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was impatient, fickle, wrathful and hard to manage; by the working of fate his brothers were born of the same kind."}},{"n":29,"text":"शकुनिर्मातुलश्चैव कर्णश्च परमः सखा ।\nसमुत्पन्ना विनाशार्थं पृथिव्यां सहिता नृपाः ।\nएतमर्थं महाबाहो नारदो वेद तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His uncle Shakuni and his dearest friend Karna were born together with kings for the earth's destruction. Narada knows the truth of this, mighty-armed."}},{"n":30,"text":"आत्मापराधात्पुत्रास्ते विनष्टाः पृथिवीपते ।\nमा ताञ्शोचस्व राजेन्द्र न हि शोकेऽस्ति कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons perished through their own fault, lord of the earth. Do not grieve for them, king; there is no ground for grief."}},{"n":31,"text":"न हि ते पाण्डवाः स्वल्पमपराध्यन्ति भारत ।\nपुत्रास्तव दुरात्मानो यैरियं घातिता मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas have not wronged you even slightly, descendant of Bharata. It was your wicked sons who brought about this slaughter of the earth."}},{"n":32,"text":"नारदेन च भद्रं ते पूर्वमेव न संशयः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य समितौ राजसूये निवेदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narada, blessings on you, declared this long ago, without doubt, in the assembly at Yudhishthira's Rajasuya sacrifice:"}},{"n":33,"text":"पाण्डवाः कौरवाश्चैव समासाद्य परस्परम् ।\nन भविष्यन्ति कौन्तेय यत्ते कृत्यं तदाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Pandavas and the Kauravas, coming together, will not survive, son of Kunti; do what you must do.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"नारदस्य वचः श्रुत्वा तदाशोचन्त पाण्डवाः ।\nएतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं देवगुह्यं सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Narada's words, the Pandavas grieved then. I have told you all of this, an eternal secret of the gods."}},{"n":35,"text":"कथं ते शोकनाशः स्यात्प्राणेषु च दया प्रभो ।\nस्नेहश्च पाण्डुपुत्रेषु ज्ञात्वा दैवकृतं विधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How may your grief be ended, lord, and how may you show care for your life and affection for Pandu's sons, once you know the ordinance made by fate?"}},{"n":36,"text":"एष चार्थो महाबाहो पूर्वमेव मया श्रुतः ।\nकथितो धर्मराजस्य राजसूये क्रतूत्तमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This matter, mighty-armed, I had heard of long before and told to Dharmaraja Yudhishthira at the Rajasuya, best of sacrifices."}},{"n":37,"text":"यतितं धर्मपुत्रेण मया गुह्ये निवेदिते ।\nअविग्रहे कौरवाणां दैवं तु बलवत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I revealed the secret, the son of Dharma strove for no war among the Kauravas, but fate is stronger."}},{"n":38,"text":"अनतिक्रमणीयो हि विधी राजन्कथंचन ।\nकृतान्तस्य हि भूतेन स्थावरेण त्रसेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ordinance of fate, king, can in no way be overstepped by any being, moving or unmoving, because of the working of the Ender."}},{"n":39,"text":"भवान्धर्मपरो यत्र बुद्धिश्रेष्ठश्च भारत ।\nमुह्यते प्राणिनां ज्ञात्वा गतिं चागतिमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are devoted to dharma and the best in understanding, yet you are bewildered, though you know the coming and going of creatures."}},{"n":40,"text":"त्वां तु शोकेन संतप्तं मुह्यमानं मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nज्ञात्वा युधिष्ठिरो राजा प्राणानपि परित्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing you consumed by grief and repeatedly bewildered, King Yudhishthira might even give up his life."}},{"n":41,"text":"कृपालुर्नित्यशो वीरस्तिर्यग्योनिगतेष्वपि ।\nस कथं त्वयि राजेन्द्र कृपां वै न करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is ever compassionate, the hero, even to animals. How then would he not show compassion to you, king?"}},{"n":42,"text":"मम चैव नियोगेन विधेश्चाप्यनिवर्तनात् ।\nपाण्डवानां च कारुण्यात्प्राणान्धारय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"By my command, because fate cannot be turned back, and out of pity for the Pandavas, sustain your life, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":43,"text":"एवं ते वर्तमानस्य लोके कीर्तिर्भविष्यति ।\nधर्मश्च सुमहांस्तात तप्तं स्याच्च तपश्चिरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you live so, glory will be yours in the world, great dharma will come to you, dear son, and you will have performed long austerity."}},{"n":44,"text":"पुत्रशोकसमुत्पन्नं हुताशं ज्वलितं यथा ।\nप्रज्ञाम्भसा महाराज निर्वापय सदा सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quench with the water of wisdom, always and ever, the blazing fire that has arisen from grief for your sons, great king."}},{"n":45,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु वचनं व्यासस्यामिततेजसः ।\nमुहूर्तं समनुध्याय धृतराष्ट्रोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words of Vyasa of immeasurable splendor, Dhritarashtra thought for a moment and then spoke."}},{"n":46,"text":"महता शोकजालेन प्रणुन्नोऽस्मि द्विजोत्तम ।\nनात्मानमवबुध्यामि मुह्यमानो मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am driven by a great net of sorrow, best of brahmins. Repeatedly bewildered, I cannot gather myself."}},{"n":47,"text":"इदं तु वचनं श्रुत्वा तव दैवनियोगजम् ।\nधारयिष्याम्यहं प्राणान्यतिष्ये च नशोचितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But having heard your words, born of the ordinance of fate, I will keep myself alive and try not to grieve."}},{"n":48,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु वचनं व्यासः सत्यवतीसुतः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य राजेन्द्र तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from Dhritarashtra, king, Vyasa, son of Satyavati, vanished right there."}}]}]}